{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2161-11-22 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I'm Dr. Lee, one of the hospitalists. I understand you've been having trouble with thick green secretions from your trach for about five days now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2161-11-22 10:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. They’re dark green and really thick. I can’t clear them well, and I’ve been getting short of breath just walking to the bathroom."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2161-11-22 10:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you mentioned some chills and nausea too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2161-11-22 10:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just occasional chills—didn’t check my temperature. The nausea comes and goes, so I haven’t been eating much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2161-11-22 10:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. Any fever, chest pain, or swelling in your legs?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2161-11-22 10:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No swelling. But I do have that same right-sided chest pain I always get—it’s not worse, and pressing on it makes it hurt, so I think it’s musculoskeletal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2161-11-22 10:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Got it. We’ve reviewed your chest X-ray from this morning. It shows your trach and port are in place, no signs of pneumonia or fluid. Lung volumes are a bit low, but that’s common with your history."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2161-11-22 10:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not an infection? I was worried because of the green color."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2161-11-22 10:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Green secretions can happen with chronic bronchitis even without infection. Your labs show normal white blood cell count, and your sputum culture only grew normal mouth bacteria, so we don’t think you need antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2161-11-22 10:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, that’s a relief. But why are the secretions so bad now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2161-11-22 10:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Given your history of tracheobronchomalacia, it could be related to airway narrowing. Your pulmonologist wants to do a bronchoscopy to look inside and see what’s going on."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2161-11-22 10:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "When will that happen?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2161-11-22 10:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Tomorrow morning. In the meantime, we’ll give you albuterol nebs, montelukast, and Mucinex to help loosen secretions and keep your airways open."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2161-11-22 10:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my regular meds—should I keep taking them?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2161-11-22 10:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve restarted your omeprazole, ranitidine, fluoxetine, and the others. We’ll also check your blood work more closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2161-11-22 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My iron was low last time. Is it still?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2161-11-22 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your hemoglobin is a bit low, and ferritin is 16—quite low. We’ll start you on ferrous sulfate 325 mg daily. We’ll look into why later, but for now, we want to support your levels."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2161-11-22 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright. I’ll take it with orange juice like before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2161-11-23 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You did well overnight. No shortness of breath, and your oxygen stayed at 100% on room air."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2161-11-23 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. I feel a little better—secretions are thinner today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2161-11-23 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. The bronchoscopy is scheduled for later this morning. The interventional pulmonologist will check for any narrowing or stenosis in your airway."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2161-11-23 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I be asleep?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2161-11-23 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ll be under sedation. It’s a quick procedure, and they’ll watch your breathing closely. You have a trach, so they’ll go in through that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2161-11-23 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I trust them. Just want to breathe easier."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2161-11-23 13:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, you’re back. How are you feeling after the bronchoscopy?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2161-11-23 13:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A bit groggy, but okay. Did they find anything?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2161-11-23 13:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. They saw supraglottic stenosis—some narrowing above your vocal cords. Because of that, they decided to downsize your stent from size 7 to 6 to help with airflow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2161-11-23 13:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will that help with the secretions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2161-11-23 13:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It should. A better-fitting stent will improve airflow and make it easier to clear secretions. No other interventions were needed today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2161-11-23 13:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. Do I need another procedure soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2161-11-23 13:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not right now. You’ll follow up with interventional pulmonology in a few weeks and also with ENT at Mass Eye and Ear."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2161-11-24 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your breathing has improved. You walked down the hall earlier and your oxygen stayed above 97%."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2161-11-24 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel much better. No thick secretions today at all."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2161-11-24 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s excellent. We’re planning to discharge you today. Before you go, we’ll replace your trach tube as a precaution—it’s routine after procedures like this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2161-11-24 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that going to hurt?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2161-11-24 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll get some pain medication first. It’s usually well tolerated. The new tube will be the same size, just fresh and clean."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2161-11-24 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All done. The trach tube was replaced without any issues. You’re doing really well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2161-11-24 12:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t feel much. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2161-11-24 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Just a few things before you leave: keep taking the iron daily, use your albuterol nebs as needed, and follow up with your pulmonologist and ENT."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2161-11-24 12:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my pain and reflux meds stay the same?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2161-11-24 12:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, continue hydrocodone for pain as needed, and both omeprazole and ranitidine for reflux. Fluoxetine too, for your mood."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2161-11-24 12:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad everything’s settled. I was really worried about the secretions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2161-11-24 12:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. But you responded well to treatment, and the stent adjustment should help prevent this from happening again soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2161-11-24 12:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll call if anything changes, and I have my follow-up appointments scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2161-11-24 12:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. You’re cleared to go home. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2161-11-22 10:02:00",
    "admission_end": "2161-11-24 17:02:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of tracheobronchomalacia and tracheostomy status was admitted for persistent thick green secretions, dyspnea on exertion, and mild nausea. She had been evaluated in the ED previously and started on ciprofloxacin, but symptoms persisted, prompting admission for bronchoscopy. Imaging and labs showed no pneumonia or acute infection; sputum culture revealed only commensal flora. Bronchoscopy revealed supraglottic stenosis, leading to downsizing of her airway stent from size 7 to 6. Her symptoms improved with humidified air, albuterol nebulizers, montelukast, and Mucinex. Anemia with low ferritin was noted, and ferrous sulfate supplementation was initiated. She remained stable, tolerated the procedure well, and was discharged home with follow-up planned with interventional pulmonology and ENT. Her chronic conditions, including asthma, GERD, and depression, were managed with continued home medications.",
    "problems": [
      "Mechanical complication of tracheostomy",
      "Chronic obstructive asthma, unspecified",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified"
    ]
  }
}
